# Everything the image must build for itself, plus everything it must never see.
#
# Without this file `COPY apps/backend apps/backend` does two damaging things:
# it lays the host's Windows pnpm symlinks over the ones pnpm just created in
# the image (which breaks `tsc` with a MODULE_NOT_FOUND on a dangling .bin
# link), and it bakes apps/backend/.env — database password, session secrets —
# into an image layer, where it survives every later deletion.

# The `**/` prefixes are load-bearing. Docker matches these patterns against
# the full path from the context root, so a bare `node_modules` excludes only
# the one at the top and lets `packages/catalog/node_modules` through — whose
# symlinks point at C:\Users\... and mean nothing inside a Linux image.

# secrets: the container gets these at run time, never at build time
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# installed and generated, rebuilt inside the image
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
packages/*/dist
apps/storefront/.next
apps/storefront/.next-prod
apps/backend/.medusa
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# the client's catalogue data and photography: seeded from outside the image
seed/images
seed/products.json
seed/reports
tools/scraper/.cache
apps/backend/static

# not part of any build
.git
.github
.claude
docs
*.log
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
